      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🏗️ HLD Phase 1: Foundation Concepts\nFor High-Level Design (HLD), build your foundation in this order:\n1. System Design Basics\n- What is System Design?\n- HLD vs LLD\n- Functional Requirements\n- Non-Functional Requirements\n- Scalability\n- Availability\n- Reliability\n- Maintainability\n- Performance\n- Fault Tolerance\n- Consistency\n- Security\n2. Client–Server Architecture\n- Client\n- Server\n- Request–Response\n- Stateless vs Stateful\n- Browser → Backend → Database\n- API communication\n- REST API basics\n- HTTP/HTTPS\n- HTTP methods\n- HTTP status codes\n- Headers, Cookies, Sessions\n3. Networking Fundamentals\n- IP Address\n- DNS\n- Domain Name\n- TCP vs UDP\n- TCP 3-Way Handshake\n- HTTP/HTTPS\n- TLS/SSL\n- Ports\n- OSI Model\n- Network latency\n- Bandwidth\n- Packet loss\n- Connection timeout\n4. API Design Fundamentals\n- REST\n- RESTful API\n- API versioning\n- Pagination\n- Filtering\n- Sorting\n- Rate limiting\n- Idempotency\n- API Gateway\n- Authentication\n- Authorization\n- JWT\n- OAuth basics\n- Webhooks\n5. Database Fundamentals\n- SQL vs NoSQL\n- Relational databases\n- Document databases\n- Primary Key\n- Foreign Key\n- Indexing\n- Transactions\n- ACID\n- CAP Theorem\n- Normalization\n- Denormalization\n- Replication\n- Sharding\n- Read Replica\n6. Scalability\n- Vertical Scaling\n- Horizontal Scaling\n- Stateless Services\n- Load Balancing\n- Database Scaling\n- Read/Write Separation\n- Replication\n- Sharding\n- Auto Scaling\n7. Load Balancing\n- Why Load Balancer?\n- L4 vs L7 Load Balancer\n- Round Robin\n- Least Connections\n- IP Hash\n- Health Checks\n- Sticky Sessions\n- Reverse Proxy\n8. Caching\n- Why caching?\n- Cache-aside\n- Read-through\n- Write-through\n- Write-back\n- Cache invalidation\n- TTL\n- Redis\n- Distributed Cache\n- Cache eviction\n  - LRU\n  - LFU\n  - FIFO\n- Cache stampede\n9. Distributed Systems Basics\n- Monolith\n- Microservices\n- Service-to-Service Communication\n- Synchronous vs Asynchronous Communication\n- Distributed Systems\n- Service Discovery\n- Fault Isolation\n- Retry\n- Timeout\n- Circuit Breaker\n- Bulkhead Pattern\n10. Messaging & Event-Driven Systems\n- Message Queue\n- Producer\n- Consumer\n- Topic\n- Partition\n- Offset\n- Pub/Sub\n- Kafka basics\n- RabbitMQ basics\n- Event-driven architecture\n- Asynchronous processing\n11. Availability & Reliability\n- Single Point of Failure\n- Redundancy\n- Failover\n- Health Checks\n- Replication\n- Backup\n- Disaster Recovery\n- RTO\n- RPO\n- Multi-AZ\n- Multi-Region\n12. Consistency\n- Strong Consistency\n- Eventual Consistency\n- Read-after-write consistency\n- Distributed transactions\n- Two-Phase Commit\n- Saga Pattern\n- CAP Theorem\n- PACELC basics\n13. Storage\n- File Storage\n- Block Storage\n- Object Storage\n- CDN\n- Blob Storage\n- Database Storage\n- Metadata\n- Cloud Storage basics\n14. Security Foundation\n- Authentication vs Authorization\n- JWT\n- OAuth 2.0\n- API Keys\n- HTTPS\n- Encryption\n- Hashing\n- Password hashing\n- Secrets Management\n- CORS\n- CSRF\n- SQL Injection\n- XSS\n- Rate Limiting\n15. Observability\n- Logging\n- Monitoring\n- Metrics\n- Tracing\n- Health Checks\n- Alerting\n- Error Tracking\n- Latency\n- Throughput\n- CPU/Memory monitoring",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
